Boat CLI

Usage: boat [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  onboard         Set this machine up: sign in, then only what the account still needs. Safe to re-run on a reinstall or a second machine
  login           Sign in with a sandbox token, GitHub, Google, AgentID, or email
  logout          Revoke this device's session and clear the stored token
  feedback        Send feedback to the Boat team by email (5 per minute, 30 per day)
  api-key         Manage API keys for SDKs and programmatic use
  webhook         Manage Sandbox lifecycle webhooks
  telemetry       Show the account's OpenTelemetry export: sandbox metrics and lifecycle events over OTLP
  ci              CI on Boat VMs (`runs-on: boat`). Alone: setup steps, problems, 7-day stats and jobs
  env             Manage named sandbox environments: repos, env vars, secret files, safety toggles
  ai              Manage AI credentials: profiles, keys, custom APIs, the credentials proxy, usage, block
  new             Create a new sandbox
  rename          Rename a sandbox
  org             Show or switch the organization wallet that new sandboxes bill to
  info            Show details for one sandbox
  list            List your sandboxes
  extend          Extend or set how long a sandbox stays on
  delete          Permanently delete a sandbox and all of its data
  deletion        Inspect an asynchronous data deletion operation
  stop            Stop a running sandbox and snapshot it for resume/fork. The data is kept 14 days; `boat snapshot <id> <name>` keeps it longer
  share           Share an org sandbox with every member. If it holds your personal logins (GitHub token, model keys, secrets), they are wiped off it first; that wipe is one-way
  unshare         Make an org sandbox private again: only you can use it. Teammates still see it and can stop it. Takes effect at once. Undo with `boat share`
  recover         Power-cycle a sandbox that stopped responding. The disk is not touched
  resume          Resume a stopped sandbox from its latest snapshot
  prompt          Send a prompt to a coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, pi, OpenCode, Prime Agent, Kimi Code, Mistral Vibe) inside a sandbox
  steer           Send a running turn a new message without stopping it. The agent takes it into account and keeps what it was doing
  interrupt       Stop the agent running in a sandbox
  events          Stream a sandbox's agent chat events (prompts, responses). A Sandbox that was never prompted returns nothing; use `boat info` for state
  conversations   List a sandbox's conversations: id, last activity, prompt count, running, harness/model, last prompt. Pass an id to `prompt --resume` [aliases: convos]
  limits          Show plan limits, the VM time included left, and the wallet balance
  billing         Plan, plan limits and wallet of the account in scope (personal, or the org from `boat org switch` / `--org`)
  wallet          The wallet in scope: dollars that pay overage, never the plan. Alone, it shows the wallet
  usage           Show the machine time one sandbox has consumed, and what it costs
  fork            Fork a sandbox from its latest snapshot
  ssh             Open an SSH session into a sandbox, or run a command non-interactively
  exec            Run a command in a sandbox over the Boat API (no SSH), optionally in the background
  run             Run one command in a new sandbox, print its output, report its cost, and delete the sandbox. Exits with the command's exit code
  push            Copy a local directory into a sandbox. In a git repository, only the files git tracks or does not ignore
  history         List the commands run in a sandbox, or print the stored output of one. Works while the sandbox is stopped
  ps              List the processes in a sandbox. A stopped sandbox shows its last stored sample
  host            Expose a sandbox port on a stable HTTPS URL
  desktop         Open the sandbox desktop URL
  browser         Return a browser-only stream from an existing running sandbox
  scp             Copy files to or from a sandbox over scp
  forward         Forward a TCP port from a sandbox to your machine, or the other way with --reverse
  dashboard       Open the Boat dashboard in a browser
  status          Show API health, account, plan, and CLI configuration
  data-retention  Show or enable delete-on-stop data retention
  snapshots       List filesystem snapshots taken of your sandboxes
  snapshot        Save a sandbox's state under a name, or inspect/download snapshots
  self-update     Check for and install the latest CLI release for this channel
  completions     Print a shell completion script (sandbox IDs included) for bash, zsh, fish, or powershell
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --api-url <API_URL>  [env: BOAT_API_URL=]
      --org <ID_OR_NAME>   Run this command in an organization's billing scope. See `boat org list`. [env: BOAT_ORG=]
      --json               Force machine-readable JSON/JSONL output
      --no-update          Skip the automatic CLI update (also BOAT_NO_UPDATE=1) [env: BOAT_NO_UPDATE=]
  -h, --help               Print help
  -V, --version            Print version

Docs: https://docs.boat.dev/cli-reference
Programmatic use: https://docs.boat.dev/sdks/overview
Environment (variables, secret files, repos): https://boat.dev/dashboard?tab=environment
